### ============================================================
### HTTP test file — open in IntelliJ and click the green arrows.
### (IntelliJ Community supports this. No Postman needed.)
### Uncomment and run these AFTER your app starts.
### ============================================================

### 1. Create a product -> expect 201 Created
POST http://localhost:8081/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard",
  "description": "87-key TKL, brown switches",
  "price": 4999.00,
  "stockQty": 25
}

### 2. Create an INVALID product -> expect 400 with fieldErrors populated
POST http://localhost:8081/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "price": -5,
  "stockQty": null
}

### 3. Create a DUPLICATE name -> expect 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8081/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard",
  "description": "duplicate on purpose",
  "price": 100.00,
  "stockQty": 1
}

### 4. Get by id -> expect 200
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products/1

### 5. Get one that does not exist -> expect 404, not 500
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products/99999

### 6. List all
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products

### 7. Search by name
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products?name=keyboard

### 8. Update -> expect 200, and check updated_at changed in the DB
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard v2",
  "description": "now with hot-swap sockets",
  "price": 5499.00,
  "stockQty": 30
}

### 9. Delete -> expect 204 No Content
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/products/1

### 10. Delete the same one again -> expect 404
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/products/1
